[["Sevier County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/utah/sevier-county"],["ARC or PLC in Sevier County","/arc-plc/utah/sevier-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record runs 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 14 grids May to June came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2025, on that same middle, June to July came in at 20% of normal and January to February at 45%. June to July is the driest pair at 1.80 inches normal, and March to April the wettest at 3.17 inches. Every grid shown had its driest year in 2020, with grid 22572 down to 41% that year.</p>"}
